   "source": [
    "### Which \"Four Factor\" Matters Most? In most college basketball datasets, you will find that the variables do not have equal impact. Usually, the hierarchy looks like this:\n",
    "\n",
    "### Effective Field Goal% or EFG% (40%)\n",
    "### Turnover Rate or TOV% (25%)\n",
    "### Offensive Rebound Rate or ORB% (20%)\n",
    "### Free Throw Rate  or FTR (15%) \n",
    "\n",
    "#### EFG_O: Effective Field Goal Percentage Shot\n",
    "#### EFG_D: Effective Field Goal Percentage Allowed\n",
    "#### TOR: Turnover Percentage Allowed (Turnover Rate)\n",
    "#### TORD: Turnover Percentage Committed (Steal Rate)\n",
    "#### ORB: Offensive Rebound Rate\n",
    "#### DRB: Offensive Rebound Rate Allowed\n",
    "#### FTR : Free Throw Rate (How often the given team shoots Free Throws)\n",
    "#### FTRD: Free Throw Rate Allowed"
   ]
  },
